{
 "summary": "Checkout failures (gateway 502s, up to 71.8% 5xx) are caused by slow inventory POST /reserve calls following the inventory 3.1.5 -> 3.2.1 deploy at 07:18:17Z. Orders times out waiting on inventory and returns 504, which gateway surfaces as 502. Inventory itself returns no errors, but its p95 latency rose to 4.77s and it holds most of the trace self time.",
 "root_cause": {
  "statement": "Inventory release 3.2.1, deployed at 07:18:17Z, made POST /reserve slow (about 2.4s of self time per trace, p95 up to 4.77s). Orders times out reserving inventory and returns 504, and gateway turns that into 502 on checkout. The deploy preceded the first timeout logs by about 2 seconds, and all failing traces ran inventory 3.2.1.",
  "service": "inventory",
  "confidence": "high",
  "evidence_ids": [
   "ev-190058c637be",
   "ev-5fa58511a1e2",
   "ev-51525d7035d0",
   "ev-676b84478541"
  ]
 },
 "contributing_factors": [
  {
   "statement": "Orders' timeout on inventory calls is shorter than inventory's degraded latency. Slow responses therefore become hard 504 failures that propagate to gateway as 502s.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-676b84478541",
    "ev-a461a4353b48",
    "ev-1da116a62fee"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "timeline": [
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T07:18:17Z",
   "event": "Inventory deployed, 3.1.5 -> 3.2.1, by ci-pipeline.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-190058c637be"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T07:18:19Z",
   "event": "Orders begins logging 'timed out reserving inventory'. Gateway begins logging 'checkout failed: orders returned 504'.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-676b84478541",
    "ev-a461a4353b48"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T07:18:32.643Z",
   "event": "Orders 5xx ratio and p95 latency cross their thresholds.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-1da116a62fee"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T07:18:47.643Z",
   "event": "Gateway 5xx ratio crosses 5% and its p95 crosses 1s. Inventory p95 crosses 1s.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-c000e6b4f684",
    "ev-51525d7035d0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-23T07:20:33Z",
   "event": "Sampled error traces show most self time in inventory POST /reserve (release 3.2.1).",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-5fa58511a1e2"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "ruled_out": [
  {
   "statement": "Gateway as the origin is unlikely. Its errors relay orders' 504s, and the trace self time is in inventory, not gateway.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-a461a4353b48",
    "ev-5fa58511a1e2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Orders as the origin is unlikely. Its errors are timeouts waiting on inventory, and no orders deploy appears in the evidence.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-676b84478541",
    "ev-5fa58511a1e2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Inventory returning errors is not the failure mode. Inventory's 5xx ratio stayed at 0%, so the problem is latency.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-51525d7035d0"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "unknowns": [
  "Which specific change in inventory 3.2.1 slows POST /reserve, such as a query, a lock, or a downstream dependency. No inventory logs or dependency metrics were provided.",
  "Whether inventory's own dependencies (for example a database) degraded at the same moment, independent of the deploy.",
  "Inventory request rate stayed modest (1.43 req/s avg), so load alone is unlikely, but saturation metrics such as CPU and pool usage are absent."
 ],
 "recommended_actions": [
  {
   "action": "Roll back inventory to 3.1.5.",
   "rationale": "The latency onset follows the 3.2.1 deploy within seconds, and all failing traces show inventory 3.2.1 dominating self time.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-190058c637be",
    "ev-5fa58511a1e2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "After rollback, confirm that inventory p95, orders 504s and gateway 502s return to baseline.",
   "rationale": "Recovery after rollback would confirm the deploy as the cause.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-51525d7035d0",
    "ev-1da116a62fee",
    "ev-c000e6b4f684"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Diff inventory 3.2.1 against 3.1.5 for changes to the /reserve path, and inspect example traces such as e1af7fdd63c588af3940a164158d28c1 for child spans.",
   "rationale": "This would identify the specific regression before re-deploying.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-5fa58511a1e2"
   ]
  }
 ]
}
